      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T06:52:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the review. Just to clarify, the current code converts the hardware-read CRC into an unpadded hexadecimal string rather than displaying its full four-byte representation.\n\nI verified this on the board with temporary diagnostics:\n\nRaw bytes read from VR: AE 60 E2 00\n32-bit CRC:             0x00E260AE\nCurrent output:         E260AE\nWith this change:       00E260AE\n\nThe most-significant zero byte is present in the hardware read, but {:X} omits the corresponding leading zero digits. Using {:08X} retains the full eight-digit representation. The numeric CRC itself is unchanged.",
      "parentUuid": "cca8b575_8689d7d0",
      "revId": "dcdaabf4b0a617bc748f0474a0f71453c59e8b23",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
