      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note: This changes the Software.Version string already exposed on existing systems for CRCs below 0x10000000 (e.g. \"EC3F49B\" becomes \"0EC3F49B\"). Is anything (Redfish consumers, tooling, version matching) known to depend on the old unpadded form? It may be worth a sentence in the commit message.",
      "revId": "dcdaabf4b0a617bc748f0474a0f71453c59e8b23",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
